{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFL}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFL}
 Este archivo documenta las funciones responsables de realizar los c\'E1lculos necesarios para la generaci\'F3n y renderizaci\'F3n de fractales. Estas funciones gestionan aspectos como las escalas, los l\'EDmites y el mapeo de p\'EDxeles a coordenadas del plano complejo.\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFM}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFM}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
1. julia_iterations
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v 1. julia_iterations}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFN}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFN}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Definici\'F3n
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Definici\'F3n}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 static} {\cf18 void} julia_iterations(t_render_vars *vars, t_data *data)\par
\{\par
    {\cf18 double} temp_z_re;\par
\par
    vars->iterations = 0;\par
    {\cf19 while} (vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] + vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] <= 4.0 &&\par
           vars->iterations < MAX_ITERATIONS)\par
    \{\par
        temp_z_re = vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE];\par
        temp_z_re -= vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM];\par
        temp_z_re += data->c[COMPLEX_RE];\par
        vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] = 2.0 * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] + data->c[COMPLEX_IM];\par
        vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] = temp_z_re;\par
        vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] = vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE];\par
        vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] = vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM];\par
        vars->iterations++;\par
    \}\par
\}\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFO}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFO}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
\'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v \'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?}
Esta funci\'F3n realiza las iteraciones necesarias para determinar si un punto del plano complejo pertenece al conjunto de Julia. Calcula repetidamente la f\'F3rmula iterativa de Julia:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_n+1 = (z_n * z_n) + c\par
}
\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFP}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFP}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Par\'E1metros:
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Par\'E1metros:}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 vars} : Contiene las variables de renderizado, como las coordenadas del punto y el n\'FAmero de iteraciones.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 data} : Contiene informaci\'F3n del fractal, incluyendo la constante {\f2 c}  utilizada para el c\'E1lculo.\par}
\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFQ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFQ}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Detalles del Funcionamiento
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Detalles del Funcionamiento}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFR}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFR}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
1. Condici\'F3n de escape
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v 1. Condici\'F3n de escape}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] + vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] <= 4.0\par
}
\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
El fractal considera que un punto "escapa" si la suma de los cuadrados de sus partes real e imaginaria es mayor que {\f2 4} .\par}
\par
Ejemplo: Si {\f2 z = 1 + 1i} , entonces: {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid |z|^2 = (1 * 1) + (1 * 1) = 2\par
}
\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFS}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFS}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
2. Actualizaci\'F3n del valor de <tt>z</tt>
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v 2. Actualizaci\'F3n del valor de <tt>z</tt>}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid temp_z_re = vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] - vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] + data->c[COMPLEX_RE];\par
vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] = 2.0 * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] + data->c[COMPLEX_IM];\par
vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] = temp_z_re;\par
}
\par
La f\'F3rmula completa en c\'F3digo ser\'EDa: {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_real = (z_real^2) - (z_imag^2) + c_real\par
z_imag = 2 * z_real * z_imag + c_imag\par
}
\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFT}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFT}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Ejemplo de Iteraciones
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Ejemplo de Iteraciones}
Supongamos:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 z = 0 + 0i} \par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 c = 0.285 - 0.01i} \par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
M\'E1ximo de iteraciones: 10\par}
\par
{\b Iteraciones:} {
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab {\f2 z_1 = (0 * 0 - 0 * 0 + 0.285) + (2 * 0 * 0 - 0.01)i = 0.285 - 0.01i} \par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab Repetir con {\f2 z_1} .\par}
\par
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFU}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFU}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
2. render_julia_row
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v 2. render_julia_row}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFV}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFV}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Definici\'F3n
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Definici\'F3n}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 static} {\cf18 void} render_julia_row(t_render_vars *vars, t_data *data, {\cf18 int} y)\par
\{\par
    {\cf18 int} x;\par
\par
    x = 0;\par
    {\cf19 while} (x < WIDTH)\par
    \{\par
        vars->c_re[0] = vars->start[COMPLEX_RE] + x * vars->scale[SCALE_X];\par
        vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] = vars->c_re[0];\par
        vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] = vars->c_im;\par
        vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] = vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE];\par
        vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] = vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM];\par
        julia_iterations(vars, data);\par
        vars->row = vars->pixels + y * WIDTH + x;\par
        *vars->row = calculate_color(vars->iterations);\par
        x++;\par
    \}\par
\}\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFW}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFW}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
\'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v \'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?}
La funci\'F3n {\f2 render_julia_row}  renderiza una fila completa del fractal de Julia. Realiza las siguientes acciones para cada p\'EDxel en la fila:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab Calcula el n\'FAmero complejo inicial {\f2 z}  para el p\'EDxel actual en funci\'F3n de las coordenadas del p\'EDxel y la escala.\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab Ejecuta el algoritmo de iteraciones de Julia para determinar el n\'FAmero de iteraciones necesarias para que el punto escape.\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
3.\tab Usa el n\'FAmero de iteraciones para determinar el color del p\'EDxel mediante la funci\'F3n {\f2 calculate_color} .\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
4.\tab Guarda el color calculado en el buffer de p\'EDxeles.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAFX}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAFX}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
