\pard\plain \s1\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs36\kerning36\cgrid 
Calculos de Mandelbrot\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl1 \v Calculos de Mandelbrot}
{\xe \v Calculos de Mandelbrot}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJL}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJL}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJM}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJM}
 El archivo {\f2 {\b mandelbrot.c}}  contiene la l\'F3gica necesaria para renderizar el conjunto de Mandelbrot en el proyecto Fractol. Este archivo incluye funciones para realizar iteraciones en puntos del plano complejo, optimizar las condiciones de escape y mapear los resultados a colores en los p\'EDxeles.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJN}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJN}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
1. compute_next_iteration
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v 1. compute_next_iteration}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJO}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJO}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Definici\'F3n
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Definici\'F3n}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 static} {\cf18 void} compute_next_iteration(t_render_vars *vars, {\cf18 int} i)\par
\{\par
    {\cf18 double} temp_z_re;\par
\par
    temp_z_re = vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] - vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM];\par
    temp_z_re += vars->c_re[i];\par
    vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] = (2.0 * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM]);\par
    vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] += vars->c_im;\par
    vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] = temp_z_re;\par
    vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] = vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] * vars->z[COMPLEX_RE];\par
    vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] = vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] * vars->z[COMPLEX_IM];\par
\}\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJP}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJP}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
\'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v \'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?}
Calcula la siguiente iteraci\'F3n de {\f2 z}  usando la f\'F3rmula iterativa del conjunto de Mandelbrot:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_n+1 = z_n^2 + c\par
}
\par
{\b Explicaci\'F3n:} {
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Usa los valores actuales de {\f2 z}  (parte real e imaginaria) y la constante {\f2 c}  (coordenadas del p\'EDxel en el plano complejo).\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Actualiza los valores de {\f2 z}  y los cuadrados de sus componentes para las pr\'F3ximas iteraciones.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJQ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJQ}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Par\'E1metros
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Par\'E1metros}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 t_render_vars *vars} : Contiene las variables necesarias para los c\'E1lculos, incluyendo {\f2 z} , {\f2 c} , y sus cuadrados.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 int i} : \'CDndice del punto en el conjunto de datos.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJR}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJR}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Ejemplo Pr\'E1ctico
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Ejemplo Pr\'E1ctico}
Supongamos:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 z = 0 + 0i} \par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 c = -0.75 + 0.1i} \par}
\par
{\b Iteraciones:} {
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_1_real = 0^2 - 0^2 + (-0.75) = -0.75\par
z_1_imag = 2 * 0 * 0 + 0.1 = 0.1\par
}
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_2_real = (-0.75)^2 - (0.1)^2 + (-0.75) = -0.1975\par
z_2_imag = 2 * (-0.75) * 0.1 + 0.1 = -0.05\par
}
\par}
\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJS}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJS}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
2. mandelbrot_iterations
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v 2. mandelbrot_iterations}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJT}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJT}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Definici\'F3n
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Definici\'F3n}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 static} {\cf18 void} mandelbrot_iterations(t_render_vars *vars, {\cf18 int} i)\par
\{\par
    {\cf18 double} current_magnitude_squared;\par
    {\cf18 double} escape_radius_squared;\par
\par
    escape_radius_squared = 4.0;\par
    vars->z[COMPLEX_RE] = 0.0;\par
    vars->z[COMPLEX_IM] = 0.0;\par
    vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE] = 0;\par
    vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM] = 0;\par
    vars->iterations = 0;\par
    {\cf19 while} (1)\par
    \{\par
        current_magnitude_squared = vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_RE];\par
        current_magnitude_squared += vars->z_squared[COMPLEX_IM];\par
        {\cf19 if} (vars->iterations >= MAX_ITERATIONS)\par
            break ;\par
        {\cf19 if} (current_magnitude_squared > escape_radius_squared)\par
            break ;\par
        compute_next_iteration(vars, i);\par
        vars->iterations++;\par
    \}\par
\}\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJU}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJU}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
\'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v \'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?}
Determina si un punto pertenece al conjunto de Mandelbrot. Aplica iterativamente la f\'F3rmula hasta que:{
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid |z|^2 > 4\par
}
 (El punto escapa del conjunto).\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab Se alcanza el m\'E1ximo de iteraciones ({\f2 MAX_ITERATIONS} ), lo que indica que el punto es parte del conjunto o est\'E1 muy cercano.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJV}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJV}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Par\'E1metros
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Par\'E1metros}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 t_render_vars *vars} : Variables necesarias para los c\'E1lculos, como {\f2 z} , {\f2 c} , y el n\'FAmero de iteraciones.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 int i} : \'CDndice del punto actual.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJW}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJW}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Ejemplo Pr\'E1ctico
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Ejemplo Pr\'E1ctico}
Para {\f2 c = -0.75 + 0.1i} :{
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
1.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_0 = 0 + 0i\par
|z|^2 = 0\par
}
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
2.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_1 = -0.75 + 0.1i\par
|z|^2 = 0.5725\par
}
\par
\pard\plain \s140\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\fs20\cgrid 
3.\tab {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid z_2 = -0.1975 - 0.05i\par
|z|^2 = 0.0413\par
}
\par}
\par
{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJX}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJX}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
3. mandelbrot_escape_check
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v 3. mandelbrot_escape_check}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJY}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJY}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Definici\'F3n
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Definici\'F3n}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 static} {\cf18 int}  mandelbrot_escape_check(t_render_vars *vars, {\cf18 int} i, t_data *data)\par
\{\par
    {\cf18 int}     max_color;\par
    {\cf18 double}  dist_sq;\par
    {\cf18 double}  esc_chk;\par
    {\cf18 double}  bound_condition;\par
\par
    max_color = calculate_color(MAX_ITERATIONS);\par
    vars->c_re_centered = vars->c_re[i] - 0.25;\par
    dist_sq = vars->c_re_centered * vars->c_re_centered;\par
    dist_sq += vars->c_im * vars->c_im;\par
    esc_chk = dist_sq * (dist_sq + vars->c_re_centered);\par
    {\cf19 if} ((data->zoom > 1.0) && (esc_chk < 0.25 * vars->c_im * vars->c_im))\par
        {\cf19 return} (vars->row[i] = max_color, 1);\par
    bound_condition = (vars->c_re[i] + 1) * (vars->c_re[i] + 1);\par
    bound_condition += vars->c_im * vars->c_im;\par
    {\cf19 if} (bound_condition < 0.0625)\par
        {\cf19 return} (vars->row[i] = max_color, 1);\par
    {\cf19 return} (0);\par
\}\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJZ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJZ}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
\'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v \'BFQu\'E9 hace esta funci\'F3n?}
Optimiza la detecci\'F3n de puntos que est\'E1n garantizados como parte del conjunto de Mandelbrot, evitando realizar todas las iteraciones.\par
{\b Explicaci\'F3n:} {
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Comprueba si el punto est\'E1 en regiones conocidas del conjunto usando condiciones geom\'E9tricas predefinidas.\par}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAKA}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAKA}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Par\'E1metros
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Par\'E1metros}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 t_render_vars *vars} : Variables de c\'E1lculo.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 int i} : \'CDndice del punto.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 t_data *data} : Informaci\'F3n del fractal, como el nivel de zoom.\par}
