{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Performs the iterations for a signle point in the Julia set. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function applies the Julia set formula iteratively to determine whether a given point escapes the threshold. The number of iterations taken before escape determines the point's color.\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Core Algorithm:}  The formula {\f2 z = z^2 + c}  is applied, where:{
\par
\pard\plain \s122\fi-360\li1080\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls3\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 z}  is a complex number, represented by real ({\f2 z_re} ) and imaginary ({\f2 z_im} ) parts.\par
\pard\plain \s122\fi-360\li1080\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls3\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 c}  is a constant defined by the user (real and imaginary parts).\par}
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
