\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Implementation of the Mandelbrot set rendering. \par
}{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This file contains all the functions necessary to compute and render the Mandelbrot set fractal. The Mandelbrot set is a visual representation off a mathematical formula applied to complex numbers. THe complexity and beauty of its patterns arise from how quickly or slowly each point "escapes" beyond a defined boundary.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAADB}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAADB}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
For Technical Users:
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v For Technical Users:}
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Core Algorithm:}  The Mandelbrot set uses the formula {\f2 z = z^2 + c} , where:{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 z}  starts at (0, 0) for every point.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\f2 c}  is the complex number corresponding to the pixel's position on the screen.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Iterations continue until {\f2 |z|2 > 4}  (escape condition) or the maximum number of iterations is reached.\par}
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Optimization:} {
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Escape Checks:}  Early checks prevent unnecessary calculations for points.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Precomputed Coordinates:}  Reduces redundant computations of pixel coordinates.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Row-Based Rendering:}  Processes the fractal row by row for efficient memory and rendering operations.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b Color Mapping:}  The number of iteerations determines the color of each pixexl, creating vibrant and intricaate fractal patterns.\par}
}
\par
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAADC}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAADC}
{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
